<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#pastoralism">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pastoralism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as pastoral</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pastoralism is a way of life based on herding livestock such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>, sheep, goats, horses and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">camels</a>, often involving seasonal movement between pastures. It was the economic foundation of steppe empires such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Empire</a>. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, pastoral peoples supplied wealth and soldiers to states including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pastoralism.jpg" alt="Pastoralism" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Achiwiki356 at en.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Himachal_Pradesh_sheep.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Pastoralism</b> remained the economic base of the tribal population, and horse breeding and seasonal migration sustained the military manpower on which all other income depended.</blockquote><a href="/empire/gokturk-empire">Gokturk Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Farmers grew millet and sorghum, and later maize, across varied ecological zones, and <b>pastoralism</b> supplemented subsistence in drier regions.</blockquote><a href="/empire/jolof-empire">Jolof Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Agriculture around Lake Chad produced millet and sorghum, while <b>pastoralism</b> contributed livestock and mobility.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kanem-bornu-empire">Kanem-Bornu Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>The Khazar economy combined nomadic <b>pastoralism</b> with sedentary agriculture and commerce.</blockquote><a href="/empire/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Pastoralism</b> based on transhumance, practised alongside settled farming, made the economy resilient in a demanding highland environment.</blockquote><a href="/empire/median-empire">Median Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Numidia combined settled farming in the fertile plains and valleys of the east with <b>pastoralism</b> in the uplands and steppe.</blockquote><a href="/empire/numidia">Numidia · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
